Maya Chen: Quick kickoff for the launch + webinar funnel. We need a compact SEO checklist before merge: keyword assignments for launch posts, JSON-LD for article + report, internal anchor A/B test, canonical normalization (drop utm_source/utm_medium), sitemap ping, and lead routing to CRM. Who can own each?
Nina Gomez: I can map keywords and messaging variants. Will create a small doc mapping primary/secondary keywords per post and suggested meta descriptions. Recommendation: target "inference runtime" + "LLM inference cost" on the benchmark post.
Priya Nair: I'll do internal linking + anchor A/B. Suggest two variants: Variant A = "Download the Redwood benchmark" (CTA-focused), Variant B = "Explore the launch benchmarks" (research-tone). Add top summary CTA + inline after 2nd H2. Also will add explicit rel="canonical" to hub page canonicalizing queryless URLs.
Samir Patel: I'll own redirects and infra. Proposal: implement temporary 302s for 5 days to monitor crawl/analytics, then flip to 301. Add header Cache-Control: max-age=360 during test. Example nginx snippet:```location ~ ^/old-posts/(.*)$ {
  add_header Cache-Control "max-age=360";
  # preserve query params but strip utm_source and utm_medium server-side
  set $clean_qs $query_string;
  if ($clean_qs ~* "(.*)utm_source=[^&]*(?:&(.*))?") {
    set $clean_qs $1$2;
  }
  if ($clean_qs ~* "(.*)utm_medium=[^&]*(?:&(.*))?") {
    set $clean_qs $1$2;
  }
  return 302 https://redwood.com/launch/$1?$clean_qs;
}```I'll also add a toggle in infra to flip quickly.
Olivia Park: I'll add JSON-LD. For blog posts use Article schema; for the gated benchmark use Report/Dataset and indicate it's paywalled: isAccessibleForFree=false + hasPart linking to extractable preview. Minimal sample I'll include in PR:```{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Redwood launch: benchmark & lessons","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Maya Chen"},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://redwood.com/launch"}}```Will run Rich Results test and Screaming Frog.
Jeff Ramos: Analytics notes: GTM events = `benchmark_cta_click` (include variant label A/B) and `benchmark_form_submit`. We'll push utm_campaign to GA but canonical will omit utm_source/medium. DataLayer example for clicks:```window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];window.dataLayer.push({event: 'benchmark_cta_click', variant: 'A'});```For CRM routing, include hidden field `anchor_variant` on the form so we can cohort leads.
Nina Gomez: For webinar copy, I'll draft 2 subject lines and match landing H1 to the keyword cluster for better relevance. Also recommend adding structured FAQ schema on the webinar page to improve SERP real estate.
Priya Nair: Sitemap: I'll add the new hub and report pages to sitemap.xml and ping Search Console via the deploy job. Also will ensure paginated tag pages are excluded from index via meta robots or noindex rel where appropriate.
Samir Patel: I'll add a smoke test (curl + header checks + follow redirects) to CI and a small script to validate that utm_source/utm_medium are removed from redirect target. Example smoke command: `curl -I -L -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} %{redirect_url} %{size_download}" https://staging.redwood.com/old-posts/benchmark`
deploy-bot: Staging deploy: seo-launch-ab branch deployed at 1758889300  all automated checks passed :white_check_mark:.
Maya Chen: Nice. Timeline: merge when green; run the A/B for 14 days, flip 302->301 on day 6 if no crawl issues (we can shorten if metrics stable). Samir leave the infra toggle so we can revert.
Jeff Ramos: I'll set up a quick GA dashboard to monitor CTA CTR by variant + form conversion. Will share before merge.
Olivia Park: Rich Results validated for article snippets, report schema flagged as paywalled (expected). Screaming Frog shows no duplicate canonical warnings on staging.
Priya Nair: PR opened with anchor copy + sitemap + canonical changes. Tagging @Maya for final review.
Maya Chen: Thanks team. Follow-up 20m after merge to validate events and confirm sitemap ping. :rocket:
